        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sojourner Truth, Sacajawea, Eleanor of Aquitaine, Empress Theodora of Byzantium, Virginia Woolf, Susan B. Anthony, Georgia O'Keeffe, Barbe de Verrue, Judy Chicago\n- Projects: The Dinner Party\n- Roles: abolitionist, women's rights activist\n\nFacts:\n- Sojourner Truth was born Isabella (Belle) Baumfree around 1797 and died on November 26, 1883.\n- Sojourner Truth was an African-American abolitionist and women's rights activist.\n- In Judy Chicago's project \"The Dinner Party,\" guests include Sacajawea, Sojourner Truth, Eleanor of Aquitaine, Empress Theodora of Byzantium, Virginia Woolf, Susan B. Anthony, and Georgia O'Keeffe.\n- Barbe de Verrue is memorialized as a figure in Judy Chicago's \"The Dinner Party.\"",
